---
// What rotli does, as one story in three steps (the owner, 2026-10-06: "clarify view vs where
// it actually lives … you write a note and open it in your view, Librarian puts it in vault
// accordingly, later ask AI about it and AI has indexing to get to it quick without wasting your
// tokens"). It also absorbed the former "You write for yourself. AI reads differently." section,
// whose before and after is now the File step's picture (the owner, the same day: the two were
// redundant). Each picture is drawn in HTML on the site's tokens, with the app's quokka standing
// on it; no cards, outer or inner (the owner, 2026-10-05 and 2026-10-07), and no step numbers
// (2026-10-07: "why even have them?"). Every picture opens on the same head, a label and a line
// over one hairline:
//   1. Write: the note in your view and its one file in the vault (ViewAndVault.astro);
//   2. File: the Librarian's before and after, which plays once (Filing.astro);
//   3. Ask: a chat that searches on your computer and reads only what it found (AskIndex.astro).
//
// One step at a time (the owner, 2026-10-08: the three in one scroll felt "dead and overwhelming
// with a lot of text … animate the transitions maybe even play with a quick horizontal scroll").
// The steps are tabs on the left, each a heading and one sentence (only the open one shows its
// sentence); the pictures sit side by side in a track on the right that slides between them. The
// track is a real horizontal scroller that snaps, so a trackpad swipe or a touch drag moves it
// too. Once the section is on screen it plays through the three on its own, once, at each step's
// own pace (src/themeCycle.ts, STORY_MS); a hover holds it, and a tab, an arrow key, or a swipe
// takes over for good. Nothing is tied to the vertical scroll. Reduced motion: no autoplay, no
// slide, the tabs still switch. Without script the three pictures stack, all visible.
//
// Every claim is a contract's (docs/design/landing-layout-2026-10-05.md lists them): views are
// reference projections, never stores, and a note's place in Main never follows its file
// (memex-data-contract.md, "One physical home, many views"); the Librarian is optional and
// Mac-only, moves files to wiki/<area>/ and writes only its declared fields, never the body
// ("Metadata ownership"); the AI searches locally and reads only selected notes, never the
// whole vault ("Master memory retrieval").
// Under the steps, "What is an LLM wiki?" in two sentences, with Karpathy's gist as the source.
import AskIndex from './AskIndex.astro';
import Filing from './Filing.astro';
import ViewAndVault from './ViewAndVault.astro';

/** Andrej Karpathy's "LLM Wiki" gist (2026-04-04), the source of the term. */
const LLM_WIKI_SOURCE = 'https://gist.github.com/karpathy/442a6bf555914893e9891c11519de94f';

const steps = [
  { id: 'write', short: 'Write', title: 'Write in your view', copy: 'A view arranges your notes. It never copies them.' },
  {
    id: 'file',
    short: 'File',
    title: 'The Librarian files it',
    copy: 'When it’s on, it moves the file and adds tags and links. It never changes your words.',
  },
  {
    id: 'ask',
    short: 'Ask',
    title: 'Ask, and AI goes straight to it',
    copy: 'rotli searches on your computer, so the AI reads only the few notes that matter.',
  },
] as const;
---

<section class="section overview" id="features" aria-labelledby="overview-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="section-head" data-reveal>
      <h2 class="section-title" id="overview-title">Write it down. <span class="inked">rotli puts it away.</span></h2>
      <p class="section-lede">You write in a view. Each file lives once, in your vault: the folder you chose.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="story" data-story data-reveal>
      <div class="story-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="How rotli works" aria-orientation="vertical">
        {
          steps.map((step, index) => (
            <button
              type="button"
              class="story-tab"
              role="tab"
              id={`story-tab-${step.id}`}
              aria-controls={`story-${step.id}`}
              aria-selected={index === 0 ? 'true' : 'false'}
              aria-labelledby={`story-title-${step.id}`}
              aria-describedby={`story-copy-${step.id}`}
              tabindex={index === 0 ? 0 : -1}
            >
              <span class="story-title" id={`story-title-${step.id}`}>
                <span class="title-long">{step.title}</span>
                <span class="title-short" aria-hidden="true">
                  {step.short}
                </span>
              </span>
              <span class="story-copy" id={`story-copy-${step.id}`}>
                <span>{step.copy}</span>
              </span>
              <span class="story-clock" aria-hidden="true" />
            </button>
          ))
        }
      </div>
      <!-- Narrow screens: the open step's heading and sentence, across the width under the tabs
           (the tab already names and describes it to assistive tech). -->
      <p class="story-now" aria-hidden="true" data-story-now>
        <b>{steps[0].title}</b>
        <span>{steps[0].copy}</span>
      </p>
      <div class="story-track" data-story-track>
        <div class="story-slide" role="tabpanel" id="story-write" aria-labelledby="story-tab-write" data-active>
          <ViewAndVault />
        </div>
        <div class="story-slide" role="tabpanel" id="story-file" aria-labelledby="story-tab-file">
          <Filing />
        </div>
        <div class="story-slide" role="tabpanel" id="story-ask" aria-labelledby="story-tab-ask">
          <AskIndex />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <aside class="llm-wiki" aria-labelledby="llm-wiki-title" data-reveal>
      <h3 id="llm-wiki-title">What is an LLM wiki?</h3>
      <p>
        Plain Markdown notes, kept organized and linked so an AI can build on what you already know instead of
        starting from scratch on every question. Andrej Karpathy described the idea in his{' '}
        <a href={LLM_WIKI_SOURCE} rel="noopener">LLM Wiki note</a> (April 2026), and your rotli vault works the same
        way: you write, and the Librarian adds the areas, summaries, tags, and links.
      </p>
    </aside>
  </div>
</section>

<script>
  import { createCycle, hover, leave, pin, resume, STORY_MS, tick, wait, type Cycle } from '../../themeCycle';

  const story = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-story]');
  const track = story?.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-story-track]');
  const tabs = story ? [...story.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[role="tab"]')] : [];
  const slides = track ? [...track.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[role="tabpanel"]')] : [];
  const now = story?.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-story-now]');

  if (story && track && tabs.length === slides.length && slides.length > 1) {
    const calm = matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)');
    const narrow = matchMedia('(max-width: 1080px)');
    story.dataset.live = '';
    let cycle: Cycle = createCycle(slides.length, performance.now(), false, { every: STORY_MS, loop: false });
    let shown = -1;
    // The slide the script is sliding to, and whether it is on its way there; a scroll that ends
    // anywhere else was the visitor's.
    let target = 0;
    let sliding = false;
    let slidAt = 0;

    // Where each picture starts in the track (the track has a little padding, so the app's
    // selection rows can reach past the picture's edge), and the picture nearest a scroll.
    const offset = (index: number) => slides[index].offsetLeft - slides[0].offsetLeft;
    const nearest = () => {
      const width = offset(1) || 1;
      return Math.min(Math.max(Math.round(track.scrollLeft / width), 0), slides.length - 1);
    };
    const slideTo = (index: number, smooth: boolean) => {
      target = index;
      sliding = smooth && !calm.matches;
      slidAt = performance.now();
      track.scrollTo({ left: offset(index), behavior: smooth && !calm.matches ? 'smooth' : 'instant' });
    };
    // Wide, the track is as tall as the tallest picture, so nothing under it moves. Narrow, the
    // pictures differ too much in height for that: the track follows the open one.
    const fit = () => {
      track.style.height = narrow.matches ? `${slides[cycle.shown].offsetHeight}px` : '';
    };
    const render = (focus = false) => {
      const index = cycle.shown;
      if (index !== shown) {
        const first = shown === -1;
        shown = index;
        tabs.forEach((tab, k) => {
          const on = k === index;
          tab.setAttribute('aria-selected', String(on));
          tab.tabIndex = on ? 0 : -1;
        });
        slides.forEach((slide, k) => {
          slide.toggleAttribute('data-active', k === index);
          // Only the open picture takes focus and clicks, so Tab never scrolls the track sideways.
          slide.inert = k !== index;
        });
        if (nearest() !== index) slideTo(index, !first);
        else target = index;
        if (now) {
          now.firstElementChild!.textContent = tabs[index].querySelector('.title-long')?.textContent ?? '';
          now.lastElementChild!.textContent = tabs[index].querySelector('.story-copy')?.textContent?.trim() ?? '';
        }
        fit();
      }
      if (focus) tabs[index]?.focus();
      story.dataset.cycle = cycle.mode;
    };

    // The clock on the open tab runs for exactly the time the step has left.
    const clock = () => {
      const due = running() ? wait(cycle, performance.now()) : null;
      tabs.forEach((tab) => tab.classList.remove('is-timing'));
      if (due === null) return;
      const tab = tabs[cycle.shown];
      tab.style.setProperty('--story-due', `${Math.round(due)}ms`);
      void tab.offsetWidth; // restart the bar from empty
      tab.classList.add('is-timing');
    };

    let timer = 0;
    let onScreen = false;
    const running = () => onScreen && !document.hidden;
    const schedule = () => {
      window.clearTimeout(timer);
      timer = 0;
      clock();
      if (!running()) return;
      const due = wait(cycle, performance.now());
      if (due === null) return;
      timer = window.setTimeout(() => {
        cycle = tick(cycle, performance.now());
        render();
        schedule();
      }, due);
    };
    const set = (next: Cycle, focus = false) => {
      cycle = next;
      render(focus);
      schedule();
    };

    let started = false;
    new IntersectionObserver(
      ([entry]) => {
        onScreen = entry.isIntersecting;
        if (onScreen && !started) {
          started = true;
          // It plays the first time it is seen, unless the visitor already chose a step.
          if (cycle.mode !== 'pinned') {
            cycle = createCycle(slides.length, performance.now(), !calm.matches, { every: STORY_MS, loop: false });
          }
        } else if (onScreen) {
          cycle = resume(cycle, performance.now());
        }
        render();
        schedule();
      },
      { threshold: 0.45 },
    ).observe(story);
    document.addEventListener('visibilitychange', () => {
      if (!document.hidden) cycle = resume(cycle, performance.now());
      schedule();
    });
    calm.addEventListener('change', () => {
      if (calm.matches && (cycle.mode === 'auto' || cycle.mode === 'held')) set({ ...cycle, mode: 'off' });
    });

    // The visitor's choices: a tab, the arrow keys on the tabs, or a swipe of the track.
    tabs.forEach((tab, index) => tab.addEventListener('click', () => set(pin(cycle, index))));
    story.querySelector('[role="tablist"]')?.addEventListener('keydown', (event) => {
      const key = (event as KeyboardEvent).key;
      const step = { ArrowDown: 1, ArrowRight: 1, ArrowUp: -1, ArrowLeft: -1 }[key];
      let index: number | null = step === undefined ? null : Math.min(Math.max(cycle.shown + step, 0), tabs.length - 1);
      if (key === 'Home') index = 0;
      if (key === 'End') index = tabs.length - 1;
      if (index === null) return;
      event.preventDefault();
      set(pin(cycle, index), true);
    });
    // `final`: the browser says the scroll has ended (scrollend), so a slide of ours that is
    // somewhere else was taken over. Without scrollend a pause in the scroll stands in, and a
    // slide of ours still under way (under 800 ms old: a smooth slide takes less) is left alone.
    const settled = (final: boolean) => {
      const index = nearest();
      if (index === target) {
        sliding = false;
        return;
      }
      if (sliding && !final && performance.now() - slidAt < 800) return;
      sliding = false;
      if (index !== cycle.shown) set(pin(cycle, index));
    };
    if ('onscrollend' in window) {
      track.addEventListener('scrollend', () => settled(true));
    } else {
      let settle = 0;
      track.addEventListener('scroll', () => {
        window.clearTimeout(settle);
        settle = window.setTimeout(() => settled(false), 120);
      });
    }
    // A hover over the story holds the clock; leaving lets it go on after a pause.
    story.addEventListener('pointerenter', (event) => {
      if (event.pointerType === 'mouse' || event.pointerType === 'pen') set(hover(cycle, cycle.shown));
    });
    story.addEventListener('pointerleave', () => set(leave(cycle, performance.now())));
    // A new width moves the snap points: keep the open picture in place.
    const resized = new ResizeObserver(() => {
      slideTo(cycle.shown, false);
      fit();
    });
    resized.observe(track);
    slides.forEach((slide) => resized.observe(slide));

    render();
  }
</script>

<style>
  /* --figure-head is the one height of every picture's head (a label and a line over one
     hairline; ViewAndVault, Filing, AskIndex read it), so the open tab's heading starts level
     with its picture's first label. */
  .story {
    --figure-head: 4rem;
    /* The app's selection wash (src/styles/base.css --selected-bg): the open note in the view and
       the vault, and the notes the chat read, are marked the way the app's sidebar marks them. */
    --selected-bg: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 11%, transparent);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(15rem, 21rem) minmax(0, 1fr);
    align-items: start;
    gap: 2rem clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4.5rem);
  }

  /* The tabs: a heading each, the open one with its sentence and its clock. A line on the left
     marks them as one list; the open tab's line is the text colour. */
  .story-tabs {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.35rem;
  }
  .story-tab {
    position: relative;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0;
    padding: 0.85rem 0 0.95rem 1.15rem;
    border: 0;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--border);
    background: none;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font: inherit;
    text-align: left;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: color 200ms ease, border-color 200ms ease;
  }
  .story-tab:hover {
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .story-tab[aria-selected='true'] {
    border-left-color: var(--text);
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .story-tab:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--accent-text);
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }
  .story-title {
    font-size: var(--step-h3);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    line-height: 1.2;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .title-short,
  .story-now {
    display: none;
  }
  /* The sentence opens under the open tab's heading (rows from 0fr to 1fr, so it slides open). */
  .story-copy {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-rows: 0fr;
    transition: grid-template-rows 320ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.7, 0.2, 1);
  }
  .story-copy > span {
    overflow: hidden;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.6;
    opacity: 0;
    transition: opacity 240ms ease;
  }
  .story-tab[aria-selected='true'] .story-copy {
    grid-template-rows: 1fr;
  }
  .story-tab[aria-selected='true'] .story-copy > span {
    padding-top: 0.55rem;
    opacity: 1;
    transition-delay: 80ms;
  }
  /* The clock: the open tab's line fills in the accent for the time the step has left, while
     the story plays on its own. */
  .story-clock {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    bottom: 0;
    left: -2px;
    width: 2px;
    background: var(--accent);
    transform: scaleY(0);
    transform-origin: top;
  }
  .story-tab.is-timing .story-clock {
    animation: story-clock var(--story-due, 6s) linear forwards;
  }
  .story:not([data-cycle='auto']) .story-clock {
    animation: none;
    transform: scaleY(0);
  }
  @keyframes story-clock {
    to {
      transform: scaleY(1);
    }
  }

  /* The pictures, side by side in one horizontal scroller that snaps to each. Every picture
     spans the track's width; the track is as tall as the tallest, so nothing under the section
     moves as the steps change. */
  .story-track {
    --bleed: 0.75rem;
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: calc(2 * var(--bleed));
    min-width: 0;
    margin-inline: calc(-1 * var(--bleed));
    padding-inline: var(--bleed);
    scroll-padding-inline: var(--bleed);
    overflow-x: auto;
    overflow-y: hidden;
    transition: height 360ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.7, 0.2, 1);
    overscroll-behavior-x: contain;
    scroll-snap-type: x mandatory;
    scrollbar-width: none;
  }
  .story-track::-webkit-scrollbar {
    display: none;
  }
  .story-slide {
    flex: 0 0 100%;
    min-width: 0;
    scroll-snap-align: start;
    scroll-snap-stop: always;
    transition: opacity 360ms ease;
  }
  .story-slide > :global(figure) {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 62rem;
  }
  .story[data-live] .story-slide:not([data-active]) {
    opacity: 0.25;
  }

  /* Without script: nothing to press, so every step shows its sentence and the pictures stack. */
  :global(html:not(.js)) .story-copy {
    grid-template-rows: 1fr;
  }
  :global(html:not(.js)) .story-copy > span {
    padding-top: 0.55rem;
    opacity: 1;
  }
  :global(html:not(.js)) .story-track {
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 4.5rem);
    overflow: visible;
  }

  @media (max-width: 1080px) {
    .story {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
    /* Narrow: the tabs run across, the open one's heading and sentence under the row. */
    :global(.js) .story-tabs {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 0.5rem;
    }
    .story-tab {
      align-content: start;
      padding: 0.8rem 0 0;
      border-left: 0;
      border-top: 2px solid var(--border);
    }
    .story-tab[aria-selected='true'] {
      border-top-color: var(--text);
    }
    .story-title {
      font-size: 1rem;
    }
    /* The short names in the row; the long ones stay the tabs' names, read but not shown. */
    :global(.js) .title-long {
      position: absolute;
      width: 1px;
      height: 1px;
      overflow: hidden;
      clip-path: inset(50%);
      white-space: nowrap;
    }
    :global(.js) .title-short {
      display: inline;
    }
    :global(.js) .story-copy {
      display: none;
    }
    :global(.js) .story-now {
      display: grid;
      gap: 0.4rem;
      max-width: 38rem;
      margin: 0;
    }
    .story-now b {
      font-size: var(--step-h3);
      font-weight: 600;
      letter-spacing: -0.02em;
      line-height: 1.2;
    }
    .story-now span {
      color: var(--text-muted);
      line-height: 1.6;
    }
    .story-clock {
      top: -2px;
      bottom: auto;
      left: 0;
      right: 0;
      width: auto;
      height: 2px;
      transform: scaleX(0);
      transform-origin: left;
    }
    .story:not([data-cycle='auto']) .story-clock {
      transform: scaleX(0);
    }
    @keyframes story-clock {
      to {
        transform: scaleX(1);
      }
    }
  }

  /* What is an LLM wiki: a short aside after the story, under one hairline. */
  .llm-wiki {
    max-width: 44rem;
    margin-top: clamp(4rem, 8vw, 5.5rem);
    padding-top: 1.75rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
  }
  .llm-wiki h3 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
  }
  .llm-wiki p {
    margin: 0.6rem 0 0;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.65;
  }
  .llm-wiki a {
    color: var(--accent-text);
    font-weight: 600;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-color: var(--accent);
    text-underline-offset: 0.2em;
  }

  /* The quokka hops onto its picture as the picture opens (the first, once the story is
     revealed, not while the visitor is still on the hero). */
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
    .story:global(.is-visible) .story-slide[data-active] :global(.quokka) {
      animation: hop 760ms cubic-bezier(0.34, 1.5, 0.64, 1) 260ms backwards;
      transform-origin: 50% 100%;
    }
  }
  @keyframes hop {
    0% {
      transform: translateY(18px) scale(0.9, 1.08);
    }
    60% {
      transform: translateY(-5px) scale(1, 1);
    }
    80% {
      transform: translateY(0) scale(1.06, 0.93);
    }
  }
</style>
